#R Regression Model Analysis in Power BI - Age vs. Marketing Plan (encoded numerically)

#This regression analysis explores the relationship between Patient Age and Marketing Plan enrollment by converting categorical plan types into numeric values for modeling. The regression line slopes upward, indicating a positive association: patients enrolled in higher-coded marketing plans tend to be older on average.

#The inclusion of a 95% confidence interval around the regression line highlights the certainty of the slope estimate, with a relatively narrow interval reflecting a reliable positive trend.

#This visualization demonstrates how regression can be applied to categorical-to-numeric data, making it a practical example of turning qualitative variables into quantitative insights for analysis.

#Findings: The regression analysis suggests that patients aged 40 and older are more likely to participate in higher-coded marketing plans, indicating a positive age-related trend. Adding the marketing plan categories along the x-axis with patient counts would provide further context by showing not only the age distribution but also which marketing plans are most widely adopted.

library(dplyr)
library(ggplot2)
dataset <- dataset %>% mutate(`Marketing Plans` = factor(`Marketing Plans`))
plan_counts <- dataset %>%
  group_by(`Marketing Plans`) %>%
  summarise(n = n(), .groups = "drop") %>%
  mutate(MarketingPlanNum = as.numeric(`Marketing Plans`))
dataset <- dataset %>%
  mutate(MarketingPlanNum = as.numeric(`Marketing Plans`))
ggplot(dataset, aes(x = MarketingPlanNum, y = Age)) +
  geom_point(alpha = 0.4) +
  geom_smooth(method = "lm", se = TRUE, color = "blue") +
  scale_x_continuous(breaks = 1:length(levels(dataset$`Marketing Plans`)),
                     labels = levels(dataset$`Marketing Plans`)) +
  geom_text(data = plan_counts,
            aes(x = MarketingPlanNum, y = max(dataset$Age) + 5, label = paste0("n=", n)),
            inherit.aes = FALSE, fontface = "bold", color = "blue") +
  labs(#title = "Shows a positive relationship between age and marketing plan enrollment",
       x = "Marketing Plans", y = "Patient Age") +
  theme_minimal() +
  theme(plot.title = element_text(size = 18, face = "bold"))
